# fixedbugs, defect 584, lane b19-dep, 2026-10-10 (panel 208's R1).
#
# SYMPTOM: a record its header marks `deprecated`, a parameter's type and
# built in `main`: clang printed its warning at the program's signature and
# at `main`'s prologue temporary of the record, a line no author wrote
# (panel 208's compiler-engineer, s3).
#
# FIX: `-Wdeprecated-declarations`, `-Wdeprecated-pragma` and
# `-Wattribute-warning` are ignored over the whole unit after the groups'
# close, the program's own lines as the compiler's (`emit/deprecation.hero`,
# panel 208's R1): a deprecation is advice about a program, not a mistake in
# it, and this language has no warning level.

extern "fixedbugs-584-a-deprecated-record-in-a-signature-builds-silent.h"
    record OldPair tag old_pair
        a: i64

function first(p: OldPair) -> i64
    return p.a

function main()
    print(first(p: OldPair(a: 4)))
